  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two point particles are separated by a distance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"x\"></span>. The mass of particles is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100m\"></span> respectively and the charge on the particles is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"75q\"></span> respectively. The magnitude of the electric force that acts between the particles is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10^{36}\"></span> times larger than the magnitude of the gravitational force that acts between the particles. What is the best estimate for the magnitude of the ratio <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{m}{q}\"></span>?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10^{-4}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10^{-8}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10^{-12}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10^{-16}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
